      "source_example_id": "e-10994",
      "knowledge_point": "Calculating the Determinant of a Matrix With A Zero Row/Column or Two Identical Rows/Columns",
      "kp_id": "e-10994"
    },
    "q-42470": {
      "dom_id": "step-q42470",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Find $6det(A)-2det(B)$, where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & 3 & 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 1 & 2 & 9 \\\\ 1 & 7 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}3\\sqrt{2} & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- Since $A$ has two identical rows, we obtain\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 7 & 3 & 2 \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & 1 & 2 & 9 \\\\ 1 & 7 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\,⟹\\,det(A)=0.\n$$\n\n- Since $B$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix, its determinant is:\n\n$$\ndet(B)=3\\sqrt{2}\\cdot 0-1\\cdot 3=-3\n$$\n\nTherefore, $6det(A)-2det(B)=6\\cdot 0-2\\cdot (-3)=6.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
